    {
      "id": 16,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Operating policy",
      "transparent": true,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 41,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 9
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### Severity & noise control\n**Critical:** target/HTTP outage, >20% solve 5xx, acceptance gate failure, delivery failures. **Warning:** >5% solve 5xx, p95 >30s, queue >4, RSS >5.5 GiB, pipeline failure/stall, reload or heartbeat failure.\n\nTraffic-based rules require minimum request volume; alerts have hold durations. Critical incidents inhibit warnings for the same component. Scrape outages inhibit duplicate HTTP readiness alerts. Alerts group by name, component, service and stage; critical reminders repeat hourly, warnings every four hours.\n\n### Safe delivery drill\nRun `.venv/bin/python scripts/verify_monitoring.py --drill` from the project folder. It briefly enables an auto-expiring synthetic metric, waits for **firing** delivery, disables it, and verifies **resolved** delivery. It does not stop application services. For maintenance, create a bounded silence in Alertmanager; inspect and remove it when done."
      }
    }
  ]
